{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1475741-big-ships-need-deck-plans","id":1475741,"title":"Big Ships Need Deck Plans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-03T10:53:30-08:00","id":1475741,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Big Ships Need Deck Plans","content":"So, I recently bought Leviathan Mabuhay and was looking through it and I must say, it really disappointed me.<br /> <br /> Now, lemme start first by chastising myself publicly. I should know better. OPP is basically the child of White Wolf, and White Wolf has never prided itself on technical stuff with fiddly bits. Now, OPP has gotten MUCH better in that regard, particularly with game mechanics (Thank GAWD somebody finally realized that clear, concise and comprehensive rules are the most useful way to stop arguments at the table....) but you can still see the marks of their heritage sometimes.<br /> <br /> My friends, Sci-fi, in many ways more than any other fictional genre, is a &quot;show-me&quot; universe. If you say &quot;Ninja&quot; to someone, they can picture a Ninja. They can go to the internet and look up a Ninja. Same with a sword or a warhorse or even an Orc, because basically the concept of Orcs have been around long enough that everybody has a rough idea what an Orc is.<br /> <br /> Now try &quot;Noetically Powered Tesser Drive Jumpship&quot;. No? How about &quot;Orgotek Scarab aerospace Frigate (I think they're still called Frigates)&quot; or &quot;BioVARG&quot;? Yes, I'm being a little unfair here. Presumably all they have to do is read the information in the books concerning the thingummies in question, but if you have five different VARGs made by five different Mercantile Concerns, sooner or later, numbers alone won't paint the whole picture. They'll seem interchangeable.<br /> <br /> Now, look, I'm no fool. Art costs money. These days, I'm pretty sure that before printing, art is the highest cost of any TTRPG. But in many cases it either makes or breaks the game. Especially when it comes to something like the Mabuhay.<br /> <br /> The thing is organic, looks like a flower and an insect at the same time. Very pretty. Wonderful.<br /> <br /> Where does the Captain sit? Where do the crew sleep? How many to a berth? Where are the weapons kept? If the vehicle stores drones and/or missiles, where are they? What do the corridors look like? How wide are they? Who gets exterior viewports? What do they look like? Are there lifts that can take you from deck to deck in the Mabuhay?<br /> <br /> And yes, of course I could settle all that out myself. I could *also* have created all those lovely NPC's myself. I could have created the Mabuhay's physical stats myself. Instead, I traded my money for what I hoped would be a well rounded look at the jumpship. Instead, what I got was basically a list of NPC's, some numbers for the jumpship and a few adventure ideas.<br /> <br /> I have a problem with the Orgotek Scarab that's almost as bad. We *sort* of have deck plans for the Scarab, but they're at best obscure and at worst of no use.<br /> <br /> Art is where a game distinguishes itself from the also-rans. Art is what gives a game it's soul on paper. Without art, all you have is math. Words will never do what a picture can.<br /> <br /> I very much hope that future supplements do larger ships better justice. Surely they deserve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21614-corradus","name":"Corradus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T16:03:06-08:00","id":1475751,"title":"","content":"I believe that is a Storypath Nexus book, meaning it is probably fan made rather than an official product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T17:01:49-08:00","id":1475754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1475741-big-ships-need-deck-plans?p=1475751#post1475751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that is a Storypath Nexus book, meaning it is probably fan made rather than an official product.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wellll, don't I feel stupid. Though in spirit, I'm still correct. There's nowhere near enough images of cool looking tech - bio or hard. And big ships do need deck plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21614-corradus","name":"Corradus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T19:59:32-08:00","id":1475761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corradus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1475741-big-ships-need-deck-plans?p=1475754#post1475754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wellll, don't I feel stupid. Though in spirit, I'm still correct. There's nowhere near enough images of cool looking tech - bio or hard. And big ships do need deck plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you in all of this. I LOVE deck plans for RPG ships. It helps with the immersion. And art for ships, Mecha and other gadgets are very important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpa